293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The premise of European data-protection law is that disclosure enables choice: that a person, informed by the privacy policy and asked through the consent banner, can meaningfully decide. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (This study tested that premise against evidence. The disclosure is unreadable, the user would need to spend 35 hours to read the privacy policies once and the consent is largely taken before it is asked, with no way to refuse on most sites. But the central finding is that the quality of what a company writes bears no measurable relationship to what its site does. Across three independent behaviours, the correlation is statistically indistinguishable from noise.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The results from this report are not evidence that policies lie, nor a claim of causation, and it is constrained by an instrument whose narrow scoring range attenuates the very correlation we sought. We show however that a policy quality cannot be used as a proxy for conduct. The document and the behaviour carry independent information, and only one of them can be measured without reading 35 hours of prose.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The compliance apparatus European users meet every day, sch as the policy, the banner, the disclosure is not connected to the conduct it purports to govern.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Improving the disclosure by making policies clearer or banners friendlier, addresses the half of the problem that is already visible while leaving the half that matters untouched. If the goal is for people to know what is done with their data, the answer is not better documents. It is tools that allow them to own their decisions and understand their choices.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (A well-written privacy policy is not evidence of privacy-respecting behaviour. It is evidence of a well-written privacy policy.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
